  "body": "Stacked on #3472 (merge #3472 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nJudge an ordinary axial spot cone at the measured part top.\nUse a separate optional `VerifyContext::rim_top_z` bound for finished hole walls.\nKeep the stock top for rapid and collision checks.\nKeep the nominal cutter radius for invalid caps, lateral feeds, and untrusted cutter geometry.\nOther callers retain the stock-top fallback.\n\nThe synthetic case has a part top at Z12 and a stock top at Z13.\nAn 8 mm, 90-degree spot with its tip at Z10 now verifies and posts.\nIts radius is 2 mm at the part top, inside the 2.5 mm hole radius.\nA spot with its tip at Z9 still gives a gouge warning and blocks posting.\n\nThe gate also found one stale catalog assertion inherited from #3472.\nUpdate its expected part-off Z from 13.5 to 12.\nThis matches the parent's corrected kerf and existing golden.\nNo golden file changes in this issue commit.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/3451-spot-drill-part-top.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe #3020 cone check measured the radius at the raw stock top.\nStock above the finished part enlarged that radius from 2 mm to 3 mm in this case.\nThe check then reported a finished-wall cut that did not exist.\n\n## Tests\n\nApplication suite `spot_drill_verify`: 4 passed.\n\n- `spot_cone_below_extra_stock_clears_the_part_and_posts`\n- `spot_cone_below_extra_stock_that_cuts_the_part_blocks_post`\n\nVerifier suite `spot_drill_radius`: 11 passed.\n\n- `extra_stock_above_the_part_does_not_enlarge_the_spot_footprint`\n- `a_spot_that_cuts_the_part_wall_still_gouges_below_extra_stock`\n- `nonfinite_part_top_never_clears_the_nominal_radius`\n- `a_part_top_does_not_clear_a_lateral_feed`\n\nThe new application clearance pin failed before the production change with `Gouge { at: 1 }`.\nRestoring `radius.rs` from `upstream/main` made the direct clearance pin fail.\nRestoring the fix made it pass.\nRestoring `generate.rs` from `upstream/main` also made the application pin fail.\nThat mutation added only inert `rim_top_z: None` fields so the new context type compiled.\nRestoring the fix made it pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` completed all 758 steps.\nIt passed 757 steps and failed only the stale parent catalog assertion.\nAfter the expected-value correction, its failed-step rerun passed with zero failures:\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --failed gate-logs/quick-20261122-153100`.\nThe original `import_step_guard` run passed.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe inherited compile wrapper stalled the first build.\nThe tests and checks completed with that wrapper disabled.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone in the #3451 commit.\nThe stack contains four NC files inherited unchanged from #3472.\nThe diff checks found only the parent's explained part-off changes:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/groove_part.nc`: 25 motion lines change Z-11.5 to Z-13.\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/fanuc-lathe/groove_part.nc`: 25 motion lines change Z-0.4528 to Z-0.5118.\n- `examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread/cone-thread.nc`: part-off Z13.5 changes to Z12; the duplicate axis rung disappears.\n- `examples/catalog/turning/groove-part-off/groove-part-off.nc`: the same part-off shift and duplicate removal.\n\nNo CL golden changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe original QA project and its preceding Face operation were not replayed.\nThe synthetic pin uses a legal R plane at raw stock Z13, with the part top at Z12 and tip at Z10.\nDrill cannot use a tilted operation frame.\nFramed contexts retain their conservative stock cap.\nNo UI window, real control, or machine was used.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nStack on #3472 for `operation::generate::run_job_arms`.\nThis branch does not change the parent branch.\n\nThe overlap check also found changes to that function in these PRs:\n#3462, #3458, #3441, #3439, #3426, #3413, #3402, #3391, #3387, #3353,\n#3283, #3251, #3115, #3103, #3059, #3058, and #2890.\nTheir hunks affect other lines.\nThe merge order can require a refresh.\n\n#2831 touches `generate.rs` in older history; its current diff has no hunk for this file.\n#2836 touches the same file, different function, in `tests/posted_gates/mod.rs`; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIts function is `sinker_gouge_cells`; this commit changes `region_law`.\nNo open PR touched the spot tests, the radius helper, the context type, or the corrected catalog assertion.\n\nEffort: high. No escalation.\n\nChangelog: Spot drills below extra stock now verify against the finished part top; spots that cut a finished hole wall still block posting.\n\nFixes #3451\n",
